# p_5e2b — Friday bedroom night: Omar's glasses at the desk, both asleep

On day 3 (Friday), the robot found both resident_1 (Yuki) and resident_2 (Omar) in bedroom_1 at 00:00, 02:00, 04:00, and 06:00. This breaks the Tuesday–Thursday pattern where Omar was in the kitchen during those hours. The mixture's worst-objects list also flags glasses_omar: predicted at nightstand_b1 but actually at desk_b1 on day 3 at 00:00 (twice). The per-object data shows glasses_omar is "mostly nightstand_b1 (3/4 days; 2 receptacles)" and is reliably at the nightstand during 9–17h (found 8/8), but the second receptacle is desk_b1.

This document predicts that on Friday nights (and possibly other nights when Omar skips the kitchen), his glasses are at the bedroom desk rather than the nightstand—perhaps he reads or works at the desk before sleeping. His tablet is at the nightstand. Both residents are in the bedroom. This sets it apart from p_e8b2 (kitchen at night) and from the statistical model (which would predict the glasses at the nightstand 75% of the time regardless of night).

Refuted if glasses_omar is at the nightstand on Friday 00:00–06:00, or if Omar is sighted in the kitchen on a Friday night.

